# AniBeam tracker credentials, inlined at build time.
#
# Copy this file to .env.local (gitignored via "*.local") and fill in real
# values to bundle them into your build. Both lines read it: the Electron
# build through Vite (envPrefix=ANIBEAM_), and the native build through
# core/build.rs, which also takes the same names from the environment first.
# A build with these set signs in with one click and nothing to paste.
# Distributed binaries built from a .env.local ship with these credentials
# embedded, which is intended for release builds. Anyone building from
# source without .env.local gets the guided set-up in the Trackers tab.
#
# Register apps here, redirect URL = http://127.0.0.1:53682/callback (exact):
#   AniList:  https://anilist.co/settings/developer
#   MAL:      https://myanimelist.net/apiconfig    (App Type: "other")

# AniList implicit grant: only needs the numeric client_id.
ANIBEAM_ANILIST_CLIENT_ID=

# MAL PKCE: the id is the hex string under "Client ID". An app registered
# with App Type "other" is a public client and has no secret, so leave the
# secret empty. Only a "web" app has one (the long string under "Issued
# Secret"), and then it goes here too.
ANIBEAM_MAL_CLIENT_ID=
ANIBEAM_MAL_CLIENT_SECRET=
